Just recently I wanted to eat something, and immediately I got the message
"You finish eating the orcish dagger."  Normally a message of this type
occurs when you are interrupted while eating something.  After you eliminate
your disturbance, you can go right on with your dinner.

I think the cause of this bug was the following:

Earlier I was lightly satiated when I started eating a freshly-killed
jackal corpse.  I was interrupted during dinner.  Since I was fully encumbered
I dropped my dinner and went to attack.  To have the freshest food available
I started eating the second jackal, until attacked by a kobold, etc.

Anyway, with all these rude monsters running around, I bagged supper and
went exploring again.  Since my inventory was already filled with daggers
and knives and tins and rations and etc.  I think I filled one of the
half-eaten jackal slots with a dagger.  So, when dinner time came again,
the program decided to see if I had anything unfinished.

"Ha!  item L is still in his inventory = it hasn't rotted yet."

"You continue eating item L = orcish dagger."

I don't think the dagger itself was very nutritious, but at least I
didn't get lead poisoning or susceptibility to rust.

